2026-09-13 23:13:56.186 [pg3] error: [{"id":368,"uuid":"c1dd9255-b7de-4406-9dfe-2ffa97855ddd","name":"eisy-polyg-sdr","version":null,"status":"active","desc":"Presents devices decoded by [rtl_433](https://github.com/merbanan/rtl_433) as\nnodes on an EISY (or Polisy) running Polyglot v3.\n\nThe plugin opens a TCP port and waits. An rtl_433 process <E2><80><94> on the EISY\nitself or on any other machine on the network <E2><80><94> connects in and streams one\nJSON object per line. Each transmitting device becomes an IoX node whose\ndrivers can be used in programs like any other sensor.\n","docs":"README.md","url":null,"branch":null,"language":"python3","executable":"rtl433-poly.py","install":"install.sh","developer":"peter.shipley@gmail.com","nsdata":"","oauth":"","purchaseOptions":"[]","author":"evilpete","devMode":1,"devPath":"/home/admin/eisy-polyg-sdr","devUser":"admin","shortPoll":60,"longPoll":600,"nsInfoPoll":0,"logLevel":"INFO","logLevelList":null,"customParams":"","persist_folder":"","profile_version":"1.0.0","readme":"","changelog":"","store":"Local","devd":"","discover":1,"authorize":0,"polisy":1,"eisy":1,"isyAccess":0,"fileUpload":0,"packageList":"undefined","license":"https://github.com/evilpete/eisy-polyg-sdr/blob/master/LICENSE","ip_added":"localhost","ts_added":1786235236,"ts_updated":1789179420},{"id":383,"uuid":"9b705690-e536-4327-868b-50d2b14576ae","name":"MideaAC","version":null,"status":"active","desc":"Monitor and control Midea (and associated brand) smart air conditioners locally on your LAN using the msmart-ng library.","docs":"https://github.com/evilpete/eisy-polyg-midea/tree/a856797da11429d1bd8cad27e1d072f837a7624a/docs","url":null,"branch":null,"language":"python3","executable":"midea-poly.py","install":"install.sh","developer":"peter.shipley@gmail.com","nsdata":"","oauth":"","purchaseOptions":"[]","author":"Peter Shipley","devMode":1,"devPath":"/home/admin/eisy-polyg-midea","devUser":"admin","shortPoll":60,"longPoll":600,"nsInfoPoll":0,"logLevel":"DEBUG","logLevelList":null,"customParams":"{\n\"temp_units\": \"F\",\n\"discovery\": \"true\",\n\"Bedroom\": \"ip=10.1.1.39; id=151732604872862; token=3a63d48cd5442cf21a26f98334cac5060188fdd9a8f3366ca112d4be76fb5477ac024892857024924e364bed00a7ae7c53ea84d52604995ff754f64656af229f; key=d3a2f7a0813c42bfa7ba7b5df5a90ac9ce4d0e725f144e76814a366468d3580f\",\n\"hide_drivers\": \"target_humidity,GV3,swing_mode,GV4,horizontal_louver,GV6,freeze_protection,GV10,purifier,GV12,self_clean,GV15,breeze_mode,GV17,fresh_air,GV18,rate_select,GV19,aux_heat,GV20,total_energy,GV21,power_usage,GV22,defrost,GV24,compressor_frequency,GV25,indoor_coil_temperature,GV26,outdoor_coil_temperature,GV27,connection,GV0\"\n}","persist_folder":"","profile_version":"3.0.0","readme":"## Midea Air Conditioner Node Server\n\nMonitors and controls Midea (and associated brand) smart air conditioners over\nyour local network using the\n[msmart-ng](https://github.com/mill1000/midea-msmart) library. No cloud\nconnection is used at runtime.\n","changelog":"","store":"Local","devd":"","discover":1,"authorize":0,"polisy":1,"eisy":1,"isyAccess":0,"fileUpload":0,"packageList":"undefined","license":"https://github.com/UniversalDevicesInc/udi-poly-template-python/LICENSE","ip_added":"localhost","ts_added":1789171807,"ts_updated":1789348548},{"id":385,"uuid":"3be746ea-3fd2-4865-b18d-5bfebb4813a7","name":"eisy-SysStat","version":null,"status":"new","desc":"A EISY / Polyglot v3 plugin that monitors the local FreeBSD host and reports its system statistics","docs":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/evilpete/eisy-polyg-stats/refs/heads/master/PLUGINDOC.md","url":null,"branch":null,"language":"python3","executable":"stats-poly.py","install":"install.sh","developer":"peter.shipley@gmail.com","nsdata":"","oauth":"","purchaseOptions":"[]","author":"Peter Shipley","devMode":1,"devPath":"/home/admin/eisy-polyg-stats","devUser":"admin","shortPoll":90,"longPoll":600,"nsInfoPoll":0,"logLevel":"INFO","logLevelList":null,"customParams":"{\n\"temp_unit\": \"F\",\n\"display\": \"-GV1,-GV2,-GV23,-GV24\"\n}","persist_folder":"","profile_version":"3.0.0","readme":"\n========================================================================\nThe metrics\n========================================================================\nVersion: 1.0.0\nAuthor: [Your Name or GitHub Handle]\nRequirement: PG3x / eisy (IoX v5.5.0+)\nLink: [Your GitHub repository URL]\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1. DESCRIPTION\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe metrics\nEvery driver the plugin can publish. The Driver column is the ISY identifier -- use it to block an individual line with -GV36 (see below).\n\n## What it reports\n\nOne node, `System Stats`, with a driver per metric:\n\n* **Load average** -- 1, 5 and 15 minute\n* **CPU utilization** -- percent since the previous poll\n* **Temperatures** -- CPU, GPU and disk, in <C2><B0>C or <C2><B0>F\n* **Memory used** -- percent\n* **Filesystem capacity** -- percent used, per mount point (`/`, `/home`,\n  `/var/isy` by default, up to 8)\n* **Disk I/O utilization** -- percent of wall time the disks were busy,\n  from `busy_time`\n* **Disk I/O statistics** -- read and write MB/s, read and write IOPS\n* **Network utilization** -- percent of link speed plus rx/tx kbit/s for\n  `eth0`, `wlan0` or whichever interface you name\n* **Network errors** -- errors + drops as a percent of packets handled\n* **System uptime** -- days, hours and minutes\n# The metrics\n\nEvery driver the plugin can publish.  The `Driver` column is the ISY\nidentifier -- use it to block an individual line with `-GV36` (see below).\nThis table is generated from the registry by `tools/update_docs.py`.\n\n| Metric | Driver | Shows in IoX | Unit | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `load_avg` | `GV0` | Load Average 1 min | load | on |\n|  | `GV1` | Load Average 5 min | load | on |\n|  | `GV2` | Load Average 15 min | load | on |\n| `cpu_util` | `GV3` | CPU Utilization | percent | on |\n| `cpu_temp` | `GV4` | CPU Temperature | degrees | on |\n| `gpu_temp` | `GV5` | GPU Temperature | degrees | off |\n| `disk_temp` | `GV6` | Disk Temperature | degrees | off |\n| `mem_usage` | `GV7` | Memory Used | percent | on |\n| `disk_capacity` | `GV10` | Capacity of mount point 1 | percent | on |\n\n## Configuration\n\nEverything is selectable from **Custom Parameters**.  The `display`\nparameter takes one comma separated list where `+` enables a metric, `-`\ndisables it, and anything after `=` is that metric's argument:\n\n```\ndisplay = +load_avg,-cpu_temp,+disk_capacity=/ /var /var/isy, -system_uptime\n```\n\nMetrics that are not mentioned keep their default.\n\nTo drop a single line rather than a whole metric, block it by its ISY driver\nidentifier from the table above -- `-GV36` keeps uptime but hides the\nminutes, `-GV2` keeps load average without the 15 minute figure:\n\n```\ndisplay = +system_uptime,-GV36,-GV2\n```\n\nA metric can also be given its own parameter key, which is easier to edit in\nthe PG3 UI:\n\n```\ndisk_capacity = / /var /var/isy\nnet_util      = wlan0\ncpu_temp      = false\ntemp_unit     = F\nGV36          = false\n```\n\n","changelog":"","store":"Local","devd":"","discover":1,"authorize":0,"polisy":1,"eisy":1,"isyAccess":0,"fileUpload":0,"packageList":"undefined","license":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/evilpete/eisy-polyg-stats/refs/heads/master/LICENSE","ip_added":"localhost","ts_added":1789288342,"ts_updated":1789290198}]
